{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And Shem lived after he begot</b> etc. But 'and all the days of' was not said, as was said for the ten generations from Adam to Noah, because all the days of the earlier generations were numerous, close to a thousand years, but after the flood they diminished, as it is written: 'their years shall be seventy.' And they diminished to seventy, and if in strength, eighty years. Therefore he did not bother to tally all their days." "<b>And he begot sons and daughters.</b> After the flood, when the world filled with people and was built up, it writes of them 'and he begot sons and daughters.' And so with David, who left a grown son, it is written of him 'lying down' (שכיבה), but Yoav, who did not leave a grown son, it is likewise written of him 'death' (מיתה)."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:52.966541575Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}